{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788705241407,"sessionID":"ses_f88dc29b9ffeZI04WaJVvtocST","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_a927a1034de044f794d67307","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view erlang-toolchain-empirical-research --repo kantord/toylang 2>&1 | head -50"},"output":"invalid issue format: \"erlang-toolchain-empirical-research\"\n","metadata":{"output":"invalid issue format: \"erlang-toolchain-empirical-research\"\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view erlang-toolchain-empirical-research --repo kantord/toylang 2>&1 | head -50","time":{"start":1788705241396,"end":1788705241400}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The issue number is different. The branch is `issue-erlang-toolchain-empirical-research`. Let me check the issue number via gh. The issue view expects a number. Let me look at the branch and see if there's a way to find the issue number. The AGENTS.md says the branch name contains an issue number. Let me try to find it. Maybe it's a numeric issue. Let me check git log and the issue list. But gh issue list is denied. Hmm.\n\nThe known denials say: gh issue list/search (only gh issue view <N> is allowed). So I need a number. Let me look at the branch name: `issue-erlang-toolchain-empirical-research`. The issue might have a title like that. Let me check the remote repo. Maybe I can find the number via `gh issue view` with the repo. Let me try `gh issue view erlang-toolchain-empirical-research` on the fork repo kantord/toylang.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_07723f8e9001n74XQdA7TVSv3h","sessionID":"ses_f88dc29b9ffeZI04WaJVvtocST","messageID":"msg_07723e719001dm714WUUWoVd9N"}}
