{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788705244261,"sessionID":"ses_f88dc29b9ffeZI04WaJVvtocST","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_dec473558379451e9d6cc221","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -l \"erlang\" --ignore-case -g '*.md' -g '*.json' -g '*.yml' -g '*.yaml' . 2>&1 | head -30"},"output":"./plans/opencode-rollout.md\n./plans/board.yaml\n./plans/board-archive.yaml\n./plans/erlang-target-research.md\n","metadata":{"output":"./plans/opencode-rollout.md\n./plans/board.yaml\n./plans/board-archive.yaml\n./plans/erlang-target-research.md\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -l \"erlang\" --ignore-case -g '*.md' -g '*.json' -g '*.yml' -g '*.yaml' . 2>&1 | head -30","time":{"start":1788705244256,"end":1788705244260}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The issue title is \"erlang-toolchain-empirical-research\" but `gh issue view` requires a number. Let me try to search for the issue number. But gh issue list is denied. Hmm. Let me try `gh issue view` with a different repo. Actually the remote is `kantord/toylang`. The branch is `issue-erlang-toolchain-empirical-research`. Maybe there's a way to find the issue via the API. Let me try fetching the issue number via `gh api`? That might also be denied. \n\nLet me check if there's a way: maybe the issue number appears in plans/. Let me look at the plans directory and other docs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_07724044b001bdMB06VNkHHpYk","sessionID":"ses_f88dc29b9ffeZI04WaJVvtocST","messageID":"msg_07723f959001BRDui2oV4A7g7F"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788705245733,"sessionID":"ses_f88dc29b9ffeZI04WaJVvtocST","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_bf8aaf0223be441dbf30b3c4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 170 --repo kantord/toylang 2>&1 | head -40; echo \"===\"; gh issue view 163 --repo kantord/toylang 2>&1 | head -40"},"output":"title:\tErlang backend: empirical toolchain verification (follow-up to #163)\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t170\n--\nRound answer (module-routing-and-erlang-target grilling round, question erlang-target-consideration): maintainer chose to go beyond plans/erlang-target-research.md's desk-only research and actually verify the Erlang toolchain empirically (process/effect model, selective receive, pattern matching) against real erl/erlc output. Note: a prior run of #163's own research spike tried a toolchain presence check (which erl / erl -eval) and was denied by sandbox policy (see plans/opencode-rollout.md, incident 2026-09-01) -- that is an infrastructure-level restriction, not something a rebrief alone fixes. If this run hits the same denial, document precisely what was denied and stop rather than retrying through another channel; that is itself a valid, useful finding to report back. Maintainer also flagged: concurrency will need to be supported by toylang regardless of this backend question -- worth surfacing as its own open item once this lands.\n===\ntitle:\tConsider Erlang as an additional backend target, as a design stress test\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t163\n--\nCaptured from a maintainer compose note (docs/.annotations/notes.json), unscheduled backlog idea:\n\n\"we could consider erlang as a target language too to further stress test our design\"\n\nNo investigation done yet into what Erlang's semantics would demand of toylang's design (e.g. its own take on processes/effects, pattern matching, immutability) or how it'd compare to the seven backends that exist today (Lua, JS, Native/LLVM, jq, Go, Python, Rust).\n\nWritten by the drive-loop coordinator session.\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tErlang backend: empirical toolchain verification (follow-up to #163)\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t170\n--\nRound answer (module-routing-and-erlang-target grilling round, question erlang-target-consideration): maintainer chose to go beyond plans/erlang-target-research.md's desk-only research and actually verify the Erlang toolchain empirically (process/effect model, selective receive, pattern matching) against real erl/erlc output. Note: a prior run of #163's own research spike tried a toolchain presence check (which erl / erl -eval) and was denied by sandbox policy (see plans/opencode-rollout.md, incident 2026-09-01) -- that is an infrastructure-level restriction, not something a rebrief alone fixes. If this run hits the same denial, document precisely what was denied and stop rather than retrying through another channel; that is itself a valid, useful finding to report back. Maintainer also flagged: concurrency will need to be supported by toylang regardless of this backend question -- worth surfacing as its own open item once this lands.\n===\ntitle:\tConsider Erlang as an additional backend target, as a design stress test\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t163\n--\nCaptured from a maintainer compose note (docs/.annotations/notes.json), unscheduled backlog idea:\n\n\"we could consider erlang as a target language too to further stress test our design\"\n\nNo investigation done yet into what Erlang's semantics would demand of toylang's design (e.g. its own take on processes/effects, pattern matching, immutability) or how it'd compare to the seven backends that exist today (Lua, JS, Native/LLVM, jq, Go, Python, Rust).\n\nWritten by the drive-loop coordinator session.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 170 --repo kantord/toylang 2>&1 | head -40; echo \"===\"; gh issue view 163 --repo kantord/toylang 2>&1 | head -40","time":{"start":1788705245729,"end":1788705245731}},"id":"prt_0772404510019w3KDxyAeovyyX","sessionID":"ses_f88dc29b9ffeZI04WaJVvtocST","messageID":"msg_07723f959001BRDui2oV4A7g7F"}}
